import{_ as t,o as i,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const d=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 304 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Youth Supreme Mechanism: Genius's Solitary-Dao Fate","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 304 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Youth Supreme Mechanism: Genius's Solitary-Dao Fate","no":304,"module":2,"tags":["Shrouding the Heavens","Youth Supreme","Genius Fate","Solitary Dao","Oligarchic Civilization"],"related":["08-Everyone-Has-a-Road Guarantee System","23-20% Activation Strategy Plan","17-Plane Transcendent Standards"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0304_模块2-遮天-少年至尊机制.md","filePath":"en/0304_模块2-遮天-少年至尊机制.md"}`),a={name:"en/0304_模块2-遮天-少年至尊机制.md"};function s(r,e,l,u,h,g){return i(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-304-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-youth-supreme-mechanism-genius-s-solitary-dao-fate" tabindex="-1">Entry 304 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Youth Supreme Mechanism: Genius&#39;s Solitary-Dao Fate <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-304-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-youth-supreme-mechanism-genius-s-solitary-dao-fate" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 304 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Youth Supreme Mechanism: Genius&#39;s Solitary-Dao Fate&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Shrouding-the-Heavens System (Entry 17) | Benchmark base: Documents 08, 23, 17</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-genius-is-not-blessed-but-pushed-onto-a-single-log-bridge" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Genius is not blessed, but pushed onto a single-log bridge <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-genius-is-not-blessed-but-pushed-onto-a-single-log-bridge" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Genius is not blessed, but pushed onto a single-log bridge&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the collective ascension axiom requires strong ones to feed back to Myriad Ranks; the republican axiom of Myriad Races opposes geniuses being institutionally isolated. This entry dissects Shrouding-the-Heavens world&#39;s &quot;Youth Supreme&quot; mechanism — each generation&#39;s top geniuses are endowed with cross-tier-growth resources and pressure, but most end up lonely, dying young, or making wedding clothes for others. The law-first axiom reminds: genius solitary Dao is not tragic aesthetics, but a product of institutional failure. Protagonist uniqueness dependency = medium (oligarchic civilization). The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Youth Supreme mechanism&#39;s energy waste:</p><ul><li>Each generation only nourishes a few &quot;seed&quot; geniuses; the rest of the same generation become backdrop</li><li>Seed geniuses die young en masse in brutal competition; early investment zeroes out with death</li><li>Surviving geniuses are pushed into a zero-sum &quot;only one can immortalize&quot; situation, mutually regarding each other as enemy</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Youth Supreme mechanism&#39;s regression consequences:</p><ol><li><strong>Single-generation cultivation</strong>: civilization bets on a few geniuses of one generation; losing the bet = generational gap</li><li><strong>Genius mutual slaughter</strong>: to contend for the sole quota, same-generation geniuses slaughter each other; civilization internal energy zeroes</li><li><strong>Solitary-Dao cycle</strong>: each generation repeats &quot;select seed — mutual slaughter — survivor — nirvana&quot; cycle, no institutional accumulation</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Ye Fan himself is a survivor of the Youth Supreme mechanism; his predatory thinking manifests:</p><ul><li><strong>Default &quot;Supreme only one&quot;</strong>: under world-view setting, Ye Fan accepts the premise that &quot;same-generation supremes must contend&quot;</li><li><strong>Stepping on same-generation peers to rise</strong>: Ye Fan&#39;s growth path is essentially winning out over same-generation supremes</li><li><strong>Survivorship bias</strong>: Ye Fan&#39;s success is narratively rendered as &quot;deserved,&quot; masking other same-generation geniuses&#39; needless sacrifice</li></ul><p>Ye Fan is not a villain, but his &quot;luck&quot; rests on a whole generation of geniuses being systematically wasted.</p><p>The Youth Supreme mechanism also has a hidden psychological cost: it makes geniuses unable to be true friends. Because everyone knows only one of the same generation can reach the end, all interactions secretly carry competition; all kindness may be read as exploitation. Ye Fan&#39;s relationship with same-generation prodigies is contaminated by zero-sum presupposition from the start — he cannot have pure peer camaraderie, because anyone close may become an opponent on the future immortalization road. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s 20% Activation Strategy broadly cultivates the backbone, essentially to let geniuses be friends — no need to worry same-generation peers will become stumbling blocks on one&#39;s immortalization road, because the road is wide enough to hold everyone.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Shrouding Youth Supreme Mechanism</th><th>Anchor Symbiosis Alternative</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Each generation only cultivates few seeds</td><td>20% Activation Strategy broadly cultivates the backbone</td></tr><tr><td>Same-generation supremes zero-sum mutual slaughter</td><td>Myriad Ranks republican co-build, no mutual slaughter needed</td></tr><tr><td>Genius solitary-Dao fate</td><td>Youth Supreme &quot;crash + quest&quot; dual route, with mentors and companions</td></tr><tr><td>Losing the bet = generational gap</td><td>Everyone-Has-a-Road, no bet on individual geniuses</td></tr><tr><td>Genius makes wedding clothes for others</td><td>Strong-one post-duty system, genius feeds back to Myriad Ranks</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate Shrouding-the-Heavens&#39; historical Youth Supremes&#39; success rate, death rate, mutual-slaughter rate</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: inject &quot;20% Activation Strategy&quot; vs. &quot;maintain single-seed cultivation&quot;</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: same-generation strong-one total, civilization energy stability</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: conclusion — single-seed cultivation makes civilization energy fluctuate violently with &quot;whether this generation produced a Ye Fan&quot;; after broadly cultivating the backbone the curve stabilizes</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: medium</strong>. Youth Supreme mechanism early self-consistent; late to give Ye Fan more opponents, &quot;same-generation supremes&quot; count inflated</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: medium</strong>. Same-generation geniuses&#39; strength adjusts by plot need</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: medium</strong>. Ye Fan as survivor, his status rests on same-generation peers being eliminated</li></ul><p>The Youth Supreme mechanism also has an intergenerational transmission problem: each generation&#39;s supremes grow up in brutal competition, so their way of treating next-generation geniuses is necessarily brutal — because this is how they were cultivated. Brutality self-replicates across generations. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s 20% Activation Strategy matters not only to cultivate a few more strong ones, but more to change the generational culture that &quot;geniuses must slaughter each other to grow.&quot; The new generation grows up cooperating; when they raise the next generation they will no longer use slaughter.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: seeds dying young, same-generation mutual slaughter, backdrop-ification</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: betting civilization resources on one seed is predation on others&#39; opportunity</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo at least wanted the poor universally to have roads; Shrouding only raises even one genius</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: under the Youth Supreme mechanism, Myriad-Rank geniuses are scarce even in &quot;being a seed&quot; opportunity</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: civilization betting on a single hero cannot support cross-multiverse stability</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Youth Supreme&#39;s tragedy precisely exposes this world&#39;s incompetence — it cannot raise a group of strong ones, only bet on one. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer: do not want one genius, want generation after generation of capable fighters.</p><p>The Youth Supreme&#39;s solitary-Dao fate is the inevitable result of the &quot;only raise one genius&quot; logic. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer is simple and crude: raise a hundred, let them cooperate with each other, not slaughter each other.</p><p>In the final analysis, Shrouding-the-Heavens · Youth Supreme mechanism described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./291_模块2-遮天-叶凡掠夺思维拆解.html">Entry 291 · Ye Fan Predatory Thinking</a> · <a href="./307_模块2-遮天-叶凡vs衡元宙.html">Entry 307 · Ye Fan vs. Heng Yuan Zhou</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/23-20％激活战略规划.html">23-20% Activation Strategy Plan</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',31)])])}const m=t(a,[["render",s]]);export{d as __pageData,m as default};
